  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through Saturday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: A trough of low pressure will progress\neastward across Northern and Central Nevada today, before entering\nUtah tonight. Periods of valley rain and mountain snow associated\nwith this trough of low pressure will end this evening. A Winter\nStorm Warning is in effect for the Ruby Mountains and East\nHumboldt Range until 10 PM PST this evening due to snow amounts as\nhigh as 14 inches. High temperatures throughout Northern and\nCentral Nevada this afternoon will be eleven to thirteen degrees\nbelow normal for this time of year. A warming trend is expected\nMonday and Tuesday. By Tuesday afternoon, maximum temperatures\nacross Northern and Central Nevada will be two to four degrees\nbelow seasonal values. \n\nThe next storm system could impact the forecast area Tuesday \nnight into Wednesday, resulting in a chance of precipitation. Snow\nlevels will start at around 7,000 feet Tuesday night, before\nfalling to about 5,500 feet Wednesday morning. Most locations in\nNorthern and Central Nevada will receive less than one tenth of \nan inch of precipitation Tuesday night and Wednesday morning. \nTemperatures will rebound to near normal for this time of year by \nnext weekend.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: High forecast confidence\nregarding the Winter Storm Warning for the Ruby Mountains. High\nforecast confidence in periods of valley rain and mountain snow \nending this evening. High forecast confidence regarding quite \ncool temperatures today. Moderate forecast confidence in a warming\ntrend Monday and Tuesday. No deviations from the NBM model output.",
